        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): use truncateUtf16Safe for message body preview truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSlack prepares a 160-unit inbound-message preview for downstream dispatch metadata. A raw UTF-16 code-unit slice could leave a dangling surrogate when an emoji crossed that boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse the shared public plugin-SDK truncation primitive at the existing boundary. The preview owner, whitespace normalization, limit, and downstream message body are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong Slack inbound previews remain valid Unicode. Full inbound message content, routing, logs, and ASCII behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added an exact `prepareSlackMessage` regression with an emoji crossing the 160-unit boundary.\n- Focused Slack prepare suite: 114 passed.\n- Focused `oxfmt`, `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh autoreview clean (0.99).\n\nGenerated with Claude Code; reviewed and improved by an OpenClaw maintainer agent.\n",
